  "content": {
    "id": "p25-q29-content",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "29",
    "prompt": "Let $f(x)=5x-4e^x$. At point $P$ on the graph of $y=f(x)$, the tangent is parallel to $3x+y-2=0$. Find the coordinates of $P$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p25-q29-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "P=(\\ln 2,\\,5\\ln 2-8)",
                "display": false
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p25-q29-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Set ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "f'(x)=-3",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ", solve for ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "x",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " and substitute into ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "f(x)",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ".",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "The line $y=-3x+2$ has gradient $-3$, so the parallel tangent has gradient $-3$.\n\n$$f'(x)=5-4e^x$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}5-4e^x&=-3\\\\4e^x&=8\\\\e^x&=2\\\\x&=\\ln 2\\end{align*}$$\n\nSubstitute into $y=f(x)$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=5\\ln 2-4e^{\\ln 2}\\\\y&=5\\ln 2-8\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore $P=(\\ln 2,\\,5\\ln 2-8)$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 84
  },
